      "text": "Earning Rate Changes on September 12th\nSalad\n\n\n** Earning Rate Changes\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nGPU prices will change on September 12th, 00:00 UTC. Before you worry, these changes include increased earnings for highly demanded GPUs, and almost all decreases are limited to specific priority tiers. See the chart below if you want to check what your future earning situation will look like. Keep reading for more context as to why we're altering our prices again.\n\nIf you're running a 5090 or a 4090, your rates are going up at High, Medium, and Low priority, since demand for those cards keeps outrunning what the network can supply. Fifteen other GPU classes are coming down, mostly at those same three tiers, while Lowest priority stays where it is on everything except the RTX 5080. CPU-only workloads are getting a raise too, covered below. And if your card isn't in the chart at all, nothing about your earnings is changing.\n\n\n** Why prices are changing again\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor once, some of these changes are increases. Customer demand for the 5090 and 4090 has been outrunning what the network can supply for months now, so on September 12th those two classes get more expensive for customers, and your earning rates on them go up right along with it.\n\nThe rest of the changes are decreases across the higher priority tiers. Our lowest priority prices are already highly competitive with the market, so those aren't changing (the RTX 5080 being the one exception), but our higher tiers were overpriced - discouraging customers from paying more for your GPUs. Needless to say, if our customers can get the same or comparable GPU resources elsewhere, at higher reliability, and cheaper than our higher priority prices - they can and will do so.\n\nWhile we can't guarantee that this will lead to 100% uptime for everyone who owns the affected GPUs, we expect utilization and priority rates to both increase, leading to more Salad Balance heading into Chefs' pockets.\n\nPayouts for CPU-only workloads are going from $0.0035 to $0.004 per hour per vCPU, which works out to a bit over 14% more for the exact same work.\n\n\n** The chart\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAll rates are hourly, shown as old → new. No arrow means that rate isn't changing.\nGPU                                  High          Medium             Low          Lowest\nRTX 5090 (32 GB)          $0.270 → $0.300 $0.247 → $0.271 $0.217 → $0.233          $0.175\nRTX 4090 (24 GB)          $0.180 → $0.198 $0.165 → $0.178 $0.145 → $0.152          $0.112\nRTX 5080 (16 GB)          $0.252 → $0.156 $0.218 → $0.145 $0.175 → $0.131 $0.126 → $0.105\nRTX 5070 Ti (16 GB)       $0.168 → $0.135 $0.143 → $0.119 $0.112 → $0.099          $0.070\nRTX 5070 (12 GB)          $0.144 → $0.099 $0.121 → $0.089 $0.093 → $0.076          $0.056\nRTX 5060 Ti (16 GB)       $0.108 → $0.090 $0.093 → $0.080 $0.075 → $0.068          $0.049\nRTX 5060 (8 GB)           $0.084 → $0.066 $0.075 → $0.062 $0.063 → $0.056          $0.046\nRTX 5090 Laptop (24 GB)   $0.168 → $0.141 $0.143 → $0.124 $0.112 → $0.102          $0.070\nRTX 4080 (16 GB)          $0.168 → $0.138 $0.145 → $0.124 $0.117 → $0.105          $0.077\nRTX 4070 Ti Super (16 GB) $0.156 → $0.126 $0.132 → $0.111 $0.103 → $0.091          $0.063\nRTX 4070 Ti (12 GB)       $0.144 → $0.120 $0.121 → $0.104 $0.093 → $0.084          $0.056\nRTX 4070 (12 GB)          $0.132 → $0.090 $0.111 → $0.080 $0.084 → $0.068          $0.049\nRTX 4060 Ti (16 GB)       $0.132 → $0.084 $0.113 → $0.078 $0.089 → $0.070          $0.056\nRTX 3090 Ti (24 GB)       $0.168 → $0.114 $0.143 → $0.104 $0.112 → $0.091          $0.070\nRTX 3090 (24 GB)          $0.150 → $0.102 $0.128 → $0.093 $0.100 → $0.082          $0.063\nRTX 3080 Ti (12 GB)       $0.120 → $0.093 $0.104 → $0.085 $0.084 → $0.074          $0.056\nRTX 3080 (10 GB)          $0.108 → $0.084 $0.0